data.reasoning_content:
replanJourney uses findRoute which doesn't check capacity — createJourneyPlan will fail with capacity_shortage if no capacity; that error propagates as aerr → returns error. Better to make replan use computeRoutes with capacity filtering like evaluateServiceability. Let me refactor replanJourney to pick the first route with capacity within deadline:

```go
routes := computeRoutes(locs, conns, position, st, start)
if len(routes) == 0 { ... exception no_route ... }
var route *routeResult
for _, r := range routes {
    if !routeCapacityOK(locs, conns, r, position, st.RequiresCooled) { continue }
    if !r.Arrival.After(req.DeliveryDeadline) { route = r; break }
}
if route == nil {
    // distinguish: any route with capacity? then expired; else capacity → also expired? 
}
```

For replan, if no route meets deadline → mark expired. If routes exist but no capacity → maybe also exception with reason insufficient_capacity. Contract replanStatus enum: not_required, replaced, expired, exception. I'll treat no-capacity as exception reason "insufficient_capacity", deadline fail as expired.

Apply that change.

